# ZenRay Houdini Short Editor V4

This folder is the durable source for the Copernicus Shorts V4 background style.

The V4 pipeline is separate from the historical `short-editor/short_editor.py` pipeline. Use this
folder when the request mentions Copernicus, style V4, blue, red, yellow, black or background layers.

## Canonical style

- Title: GT Sectra Bold, uppercase, 1.25x the V3 title scale, white in the selected finals.
- Subtitles: Archive Garamond Bold Italic, normal sentence case, English by default, white in the
  selected finals.
- Backgrounds: blue layer 01, red layer 02, yellow layer 03 and black layer 04, the only canonical visual assets.
- Selected stills: centered text with black drop shadows.
- Canonical movie: fixed backgrounds, blue to red crossfade, line-by-line Canon pop, subtitle fade
  out, no left-to-right sweep and no drop shadow.
- Movie master: 3072 x 3840, 30 fps, 6 seconds, HEVC hvc1 MOV. Browser companion: H.264 MP4.

## Replay

Run from this directory with the Shorts virtual environment:

```bash
cd /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-houdini/short-editor-v4
/Users/zenray/.venvs/shorts/bin/python scripts/generate_v4_selected.py
# Optional exploration matrix and animation proof:
/Users/zenray/.venvs/shorts/bin/python scripts/generate_all_shorts.py
```

The four source backgrounds are in `assets/backgrounds/`. The selected final proofs are in
`assets/selected-finals/`. No unrelated Copernicus reference image is part of the V4 bundle.
`ASSET_INDEX.json` records the SHA-256 fingerprint of every canonical file.

## Subtitle language

Visible subtitle text in posts and shorts is English by default. A source post may contain French and
English Markdown, but the short uses the edited English wording word for word, without translation or
invention, unless Matthieu explicitly requests another language.
